top to bottom direction
title Tactical DDD · Media Asset / source identity
package "Asset consistency grouping (interpretation)" $MEDIA {
 class Asset <<principal root>> {
  id: UUID
  owner_id: UUID
  source_key: str
  source_revision: int
  source_sha256: str
  source_size_bytes: int
  source_media_type: str
  source_asset_id: UUID | None
  operations: list
  processing_job_id: UUID | None
  deleted_at: datetime | None
 }
 class SourceVersion <<persisted value record>> {
  asset_id: UUID
  bucket: str
  key: str
  version_id: str
  sha256: str
  size_bytes: int
  content_type: str
 }
 Asset "1" *-right- "0..1" SourceVersion
}
class "contracts.v1.Source" as Source <<frozen value object>> $INFRA {
 bucket: str
 key: str
 version_id: str
 sha256: str
 size_bytes: int
 content_type: str
}
SourceVersion ..right> Source : field mapping\n(via dict)
note bottom of Asset
  get_asset(): owner/deleted filters by options.
  CHECK: source_revision >= 1, size > 0.
  edit(): new Asset; parent is source_asset_id
  (UUID only; no FK or object reference).
end note
note bottom of SourceVersion
  pin_copied_source() + stage_submit():
  new Asset, SourceVersion, optional RequestKey
  and submit outbox commit together.
  Direct uploads keep pin on UploadReservation.
end note
legend bottom
  Diamond = owned value interpretation; SourceVersion has no independent domain identity.
  owner_id: User identity + local FK; processing_job_id: UUID only, no Processing FK.
  source_for_asset() returns a dict; Envelope.from_dict() constructs the frozen Source.
  Adoption spans reservation + Asset roots; service functions enforce the rules.
endlegend

@enduml
